  "category": "side-items",
  "language": "en",
  "description": "This makes a total of 5 servings of Toasted Garlic Cauliflower Wrap. Each serving comes out to be 87 calories, 4.4g fats, 2.8g net carbs, and 7.2g protein.",
  "servings": 5,
  "yield": [
    "5",
    "5 servings"
  ],
  "prepTime": "PT10M",
  "cookTime": "PT30M",
  "totalTime": "PT40M",
  "totalMinutes": 40,
  "nutrition": {
    "@type": "NutritionInformation",
    "calories": "87 kcal",
    "fatContent": "4.4 g",
    "proteinContent": "7.2 g",
    "carbohydrateContent": "2.8 g",
    "servingSize": "1 serving"
  },
  "nutritionPerServing": {
    "calories": 87,
    "netCarbsGrams": 2.8,
    "proteinGrams": 7.2,
    "fatGrams": 4.4
  },
  "ingredients": [
    "588 gram cauliflower (cut into florets)",
    "4 large egg",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "1 1/2 teaspoon all-purpose seasoning (see note*)",
    "1 teaspoon salt"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 375F. Line two baking sheets with parchment paper. Rice the cauliflower by pulsing the florets in a food processor.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-cauliflower-wrap/#wprm-recipe-50421-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/toasted-garlic-cauliflower-wrap-step-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add some water to the riced cauliflower, then put it in a saucepan with lid. Cook on medium high until tender, about 8-10 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-cauliflower-wrap/#wprm-recipe-50421-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/toasted-garlic-cauliflower-wrap-step-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain all the water out, and transfer the cauliflower to a kitchen towel. Wring out the excess water from the cauliflower. This stage is vital - get as much water out as possible.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-cauliflower-wrap/#wprm-recipe-50421-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/toasted-garlic-cauliflower-wrap-step-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a bowl, mix the cauliflower, eggs, garlic, herbs, and salt.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-cauliflower-wrap/#wprm-recipe-50421-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/toasted-garlic-cauliflower-wrap-step-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Form 4 thin circles on the parchment-lined baking sheets. Press the dough down so it forms a thin layer. Keep the wraps fully formed and consistent. There should be no holes showing.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-cauliflower-wrap/#wprm-recipe-50421-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/toasted-garlic-cauliflower-wrap-step-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake them until they're dry and pliable, about 15-20 minutes. Let them cool on a wire rack; if you don't let air circulate underneath, the bottoms will become soggy.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-cauliflower-wrap/#wprm-recipe-50421-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/toasted-garlic-cauliflower-wrap-step-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Do with them what you will - dip them in sauce, add some meats and cheese, or toss some vegetables inside. They're really delicious with anything that I used to put in my wraps - including my Low Carb Chili Con Carne.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garlic-cauliflower-wrap/#wprm-recipe-50421-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/toasted-garlic-cauliflower-wrap-step-07.jpg"
    }
  ],
